id: pm-case-budget
title: Read the stored budget setting only when no explicit budget is given
description: "An invalid stored case output_budget (0, -1, 1.5, 8193) threw before an explicit --budget was honored, because the eager integer(policy?.output_budget, 1600) fallback evaluated first. Read the stored setting lazily, only when no explicit budget transport is provided."
type: Issue
pm_format_version: 2
status: closed
priority: 2
tags[1]: "gh:unbraind/pm-case#5"
created_at: "2026-11-09T19:46:28.641Z"
updated_at: "2026-11-14T09:58:51.156Z"
closed_at: "2026-11-14T08:45:06.652Z"
completed_at: "2026-11-11T17:53:32.000Z"
author: codex-agent
acceptance_criteria: An explicit valid budget succeeds while the stored setting is invalid; Without a budget the invalid stored setting still refuses; Regression fails on revert
comments[21]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-11-09T19:46:34.861Z",codex-agent,"Plan: apply the lazy stored-setting fallback in the command dispatch (requested budget first, stored section only when no explicit transport), search for other eager stored-setting fallbacks, and add an extension-harness contract that writes an invalid stored output_budget with the SDK settings writer and proves an explicit budget still succeeds while the un-budgeted command still refuses."
  "2026-11-09T19:49:44.629Z",codex-agent,"Revert proof: with only the two source changes reverted (commands dispatch restored to the eager integer(requested, integer(policy?.output_budget, 1600)) fallback and guardSubmitted restored to the length-only array bound), the focused privacy and contracts suites fail exactly on the two new regressions ('an explicit budget is not refused by an invalid stored budget setting' and 'sparse arrays refuse before schema parsing and only dense arrays are admitted') and pass again once the fix is restored (15/15). The stored 8193 case clamps to the package's 8192 fitting ceiling instead of refusing, which the contract records explicitly."
  "2026-11-09T20:06:17.914Z",codex-agent,"Continuation preserves the existing changes and item. Correcting the prior test exception for stored 8193 to meet the requested refusal when it is selected as the fallback, adding host output-budget coverage, and checking the array length against the remaining aggregate traversal budget before allocating keys. The earlier revert receipt will be superseded with fresh isolated proofs."
  "2026-11-09T20:17:42.172Z",codex-agent,"Fresh isolated revert proofs supersede the earlier receipt: restoring only base src/commands.ts and rebuilding fails 'an explicit budget is not refused by an invalid stored budget setting' (exit 1); restoring the fix and rebuilding passes. Restoring only base src/schema.ts and rebuilding fails 'sparse arrays refuse before schema parsing and only dense arrays are admitted' (exit 1); restoring the fixed guard and rebuilding passes. Both package --budget and host --output-budget, including unbounded, override stored 0, -1, 1.5 and 8193; all four stored values refuse when selected without an override. Invalid explicit budgets still refuse. Dense indices are checked after the remaining aggregate node bound and before schema parsing. The text-budget fixture stays below the node ceiling so it still exercises the independent text limit. No other eager stored-setting fallback remains. Focused suites and pinned pm test --run --progress: 15/15 passed. Complete npm test: 100/100 passed, zero skipped. npm run typecheck and npm run lint passed."
  "2026-11-09T20:18:38.633Z",codex-agent,"Handoff: PR https://github.com/unbraind/pm-case/pull/5; source fix e690e8ca442eb64166325a67d61e64521efc6b31. Exact source-head checks observed queued: CI test (22), test (26), https://github.com/unbraind/pm-case/actions/runs/42691665269; CodeQL https://github.com/unbraind/pm-case/actions/runs/42691665625. Automated reviews are skipped or neutral and are not approval. Full CI certification remains pending; the orchestrator owns verification and closure."
  "2026-11-11T08:21:06.098Z",codex-seams-1111,"Investigating Node 26 revert acceptance failure. Reproduce CI build and acceptance, audit every mutation seam for exactly one match, refresh only stale fragments preserving named behavior, and aggregate stale diagnostics before proofs. Run focused tests and both release gates; leave item open and release this claim."
  "2026-11-11T08:23:56.775Z",codex-seams-1111,Reproduced the original CI failure with bun run build && node test/revert.acceptance.ts under Node 26.13.0. Full preflight audit found one stale seam; all other seams match exactly once. Updated the exact fragment while retaining its original mutation and named failing test. Added a disposable-copy regression for combined missing and ambiguous seam diagnostics before any proof runs.
  "2026-11-11T08:28:54.748Z",codex-seams-1111,"The first repaired sparse-array seam matched once but its mutation remained green: the newer dense-key check also refused oversized sparse arrays. Strengthened the same named privacy regression with an oversized-array Proxy whose ownKeys trap fails if allocation is reached; require the original traversal-budget refusal first. This preserves the original length-bound mutation and proves its early admission behavior independently of the later sparse-key check. The combined-diagnostic regression fails proof:seam_diagnostics when the collector is reverted to first-only reporting in disposable copies in both packages."
  "2026-11-11T08:38:05.421Z",codex-seams-1111,"Full pinned-pm CI-equivalent acceptance passed: 73 behavioral mutations each fail the named regression and restore green, 4 linked build proofs, and 3 wrong-error-code proofs. The new combined-diagnostic self-mutation is included. Independent oversized-array length-bound proof is green/red/green (0/1/0) with proof:sparse_array_length_budget. Focused privacy and diagnostics tests pass 10/10; typecheck, lint, docstrings and identity/privacy checks pass. All checks use Node 26.13.0 and Bun 1.3.5 with a 20-minute acceptance cap."
  "2026-11-11T08:38:22.885Z",codex-seams-1111,"Correction to the preceding count: the acceptance receipt reports 69 behavioral mutations (69 red and 69 restored green), not 73. All 72 seams match exactly once, including the 3 wrong-error-code probes. The 4 linked build proofs are separate. Acceptance stdout is 71 lines; build stderr is 1 line. All other results in the preceding comment stand."
  "2026-11-11T09:20:36.794Z",codex-seams-1111,"Final local verification: npm run release:check and bun run release:check both passed all 14 sequential gate steps with isolated HOME/Git settings. Each passed 101/101 unit tests (zero skipped), one packed acceptance spanning npm/Bun and Node 22.19.0/26.13.0, and exactly 100 percent coverage: statements 607/607, branches 343/343, functions 171/171, lines 492/492. Standalone CI-equivalent acceptance stdout has 71 lines, plus one build stderr line. Full release links use 3600-second bounds; focused tests and standalone acceptance retain 1200-second caps. Tracker histories remain append-only. Final audit comment and claim release are followed by regenerated changelog and fresh tracker/identity/changelog checks; hosted checks for the pushed head are reported in the PR. Item remains in progress for orchestrator verification. A transient registry audit endpoint error interrupted one Bun attempt; a fresh complete Bun gate subsequently passed without bypassing the audit."
  "2026-11-11T10:48:02.159Z",codex-seams-1111,"Resumed one scoped review round for PR 5 at aaea545. Fetched every thread and every comment with no omitted pages: PRRT_kwDOVlkMx862Hk27 (stable validation/parse snapshot), PRRT_kwDOVlkMx862Hk3Q (independent dense-index seam), PRRT_kwDOVlkMx862Hk3H (assertion-probe diagnostics), PRRT_kwDOVlkMx862Hk2x (portable linked deadlines). The blocking thread describes mutable Proxy input, while the orchestrator also requires a same-class audit of stored settings and tracker reads; address both at their actual boundaries. No thread replies or resolutions; no changes to the accepted sibling package. The queue forbids delegation, so security boundary and bypass reviews will be separate local inspection passes."
  "2026-11-11T10:55:21.099Z",codex-seams-1111,"Boundary audit: schema parsing was vulnerable because privacy traversal and Zod consumed the original mutable object separately. The capture now reads each own data descriptor once, validates the captured child, and parses that same detached tree; inherited values and later Proxy/file changes are excluded. commands.ts captures one readSettingsSection value, host.ts uses single native settings reads, api.ts validates one complete get snapshot, kernel.ts validates that captured state, and script file readers consume their captured text directly. No independent validate-then-reread file path exists in those modules. Added real settings/tracker second-write controls plus a real input-file replacement at the privacy-to-Zod boundary. Portable links now use relative Node/npm commands and PM timeout_seconds instead of platform-specific timeout/sh wrappers."
  "2026-11-11T11:02:33.366Z",codex-seams-1111,"Focused native verification passes 16/16, including the real file replacement, Proxy array/object controls, settings second-write control and tracker second-write control. All existing test files also passed 107/107 before the final independent extra-key regression was added. Portable linked commands have a separate real-temp-tracker green/red/green proof (0/1/0), with all metadata edits made through pinned pm commands and history retained. A separate boundary/bypass inspection confirmed own-descriptor capture covers nested arrays and objects, refuses vanishing or invalid descriptors, never consults inherited elements, preserves traversal/text ceilings, and leaves stored-mode compatibility unchanged. Full revert acceptance will additionally certify independent array-bound, sparse-index, extra-key, file-snapshot and assertion-probe-coverage mutations."
  "2026-11-11T11:12:53.030Z",codex-seams-1111,"CI-equivalent bun build plus revert acceptance passed within the 1200-second cap: all 76 seams match once; 73 named behavioral mutations fail and restore green; 4 linked build proofs and 3 wrong-error-code probes pass. Combined stdout/build-stderr log has 76 lines (75 acceptance stdout plus one build line). The new file-replacement mutation proves unvalidated replacement data cannot enter an outcome. Separate dense-index removals fail sparse-hole and named-key regressions while the aggregate bound remains intact. Omitting assertionProbes from preflight now fails the diagnostic fixture. Latest pinned-pm focused run passes 17/17. Portable linked metadata has a separate real-temp-tracker 0/1/0 revert proof. Typecheck, lint and all 102 documented declarations pass. npm release verification follows within the scoped 45-minute round budget; the previously accepted sibling package is unchanged."
  "2026-11-11T11:28:11.089Z",codex-seams-1111,"Scoped review outcome: fixed. The original file/Proxy substitution is prevented by validating and parsing the same detached own-data snapshot. Real file replacement, late inherited array values and mutable object controls pass; public Unicode, dense arrays and historical stored data remain compatible. Settings and tracker second-write tests each assert one native read and retain the validated captured value. Latest focused pinned-pm run passes 17/17. Full npm run release:check passes all 14 steps: 108/108 unit tests with zero skips, one packed npm/Bun acceptance across Node 22.19.0 and 26.13.0, and exactly 100 percent of statements/branches/functions/lines. Standalone bun build plus revert acceptance passes all 76 exact seams, 73 red/restored-green behaviors, 4 build proofs and 3 wrong-error-code proofs; combined log has 76 lines. Separate dense-index proofs cover holes and named keys independently of the aggregate bound. Omitting assertionProbes now fails diagnostic coverage. Portable PM deadlines use only relative commands and timeout_seconds metadata; a real-temp-tracker metadata revert proves 0/1/0. Four scoped review threads and all four comments/diff hunks were read with no omitted pages. No replies, reactions or resolutions were made. This round obeys the scoped gate budget; a second full Bun release run and changes to the accepted sibling package were not part of this round. Final comment and claim release are followed by regenerated changelog and fresh tracker/identity/changelog checks. Item remains in progress for orchestrator verification."
  "2026-11-11T15:31:49.954Z",codex-seams-1111,"Tiny final review round for PRRT_kwDOVlkMx862Jo9v at 09806ff. Fetched the full thread comment and diff with no omitted pages. Audit found two direct Node links on this item missing a build; the kernel, proof and storage items already prefix all four direct Node links with npm run build. Script-driven revert and release links build internally. Replace the two affected links through pinned pm remove/add operations and update the portable-command regression to enforce build-before-test across all four items. The item also contains duplicate full npm/Bun release links already retained on the release epic; execution scope is being clarified against the 20-minute cap. No review-thread replies or resolutions."
  "2026-11-11T15:35:42.582Z",codex-seams-1111,"Both corrected focused links now build before Node and keep 1200-second metadata deadlines. The first linked selection passed from absent dist and rebuilt it. The build-prefix regression has a real-temp-tracker 0/1/0 proof: restoring the old direct Node command fails proof:linked_build, then restoring the build prefix passes. To keep the unfiltered issue run within the requested 20-minute cap and avoid repeating accepted full release work, deduplicated its npm/Bun release links; both identical full checks remain unchanged on pm-case-release with their existing 5400-second deadlines. No release check or threshold was removed from the project. The issue retains its revert acceptance and both focused selections. The four kernel/proof/storage links already build first and need no edit."
  "2026-11-11T15:44:50.473Z",codex-seams-1111,"The unfiltered npx pm test pm-case-budget --run passed all three retained links after generated dist was deleted. Both focused selections also independently passed from absent dist and rebuilt it: privacy/contracts 16/16, privacy/diagnostics/snapshot 17/17. The item run's revert receipt reports 73 red/restored-green behaviors, 4 linked build proofs and 3 wrong-error-code probes. No release gate was bypassed or changed: duplicate issue links were removed while the canonical full npm/Bun links remain on the release epic. Completing the four audited sibling links and the explicitly requested Bun-build acceptance next, each with a 20-minute outer cap."
  "2026-11-11T15:58:51.548Z",codex-seams-1111,"Final build-link verification passed. Deleted ignored, untracked generated dist before the unfiltered npx pm test pm-case-budget --run: all 3 retained commands passed and rebuilt dist. Both changed focused links independently passed from absent dist too (16/16 privacy/contracts; 17/17 privacy/diagnostics/snapshot). All 4 unchanged sibling links passed through pinned pm: kernel 1/1, proof 1/1, storage 2/2. Their old branch provenance required local fingerprint acknowledgement after reviewing the exact commands; definitions were not changed. Separate bun run build && node test/revert.acceptance.ts passed under its 1200-second cap: 76 exact seams, 73 red/restored-green behaviors, 4 linked build proofs, 3 wrong-error-code probes, and 76 combined output lines. The new build-prefix regression has an isolated real-temp-tracker 0/1/0 proof using pinned pm metadata edits. Typecheck and lint pass. Duplicate full npm/Bun release links remain unchanged on pm-case-release; only duplicate issue links were removed to keep the requested full issue run bounded. No release definition or validation threshold changed. Final comment and claim release are followed by changelog regeneration and tracker/identity/changelog checks; the issue remains in progress for orchestrator verification. No review-thread replies or resolutions."
  "2026-11-14T09:58:51.055Z",codex-sweep-1114,"Release-attribution correction: completed_at = 2026-11-11T17:53:32Z from https://github.com/unbraind/pm-case/pull/5 (merge SHA 794adf6f223af8efee434b2f98e8d7a1408512be); no fetched release tag contains that merge commit, so release remains unset and this work is genuinely unreleased."
